      "other_names": "",
      "local_names": "",
      "researcher_notes_unit": "AL2026: Marking as shelved because FSRU is in Türkiye as of February; perhaps it was replaced by the Energos Eskimo, or perhaps it only served in Egypt for a few months in the summer. It's unclear to me, since I wasn't able to find any explicit evidence of it arriving/leaving Egypt. https://www.giignl.org/news/egypt-scales-up-regas-capacity-with-fsru-deployments-from-botas-sefe-and-hoegh-lng",
      "researcher_notes_project": "AL2026: Ain Sokhna has two import jetties/complexes. The first, the Ain Sokhna FSRU jetty (Sonker berth), was constructed around 2015, while the second, Sumed, appears to have been built sometime between 2017 and 2019. Though both are located in the same general area, they have accommodated different FSRUs over the years. Sumed is situated somewhat farther south and features a more complex, larger layout, with what appears to be enough berthing space for at least two, maybe probably FSRUs. The other, simpler, smaller, and older jetty, appears to be able to have enough berthing space for one FSRU at a time.",
      "is_fsru": true,
